>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Onaral</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Motion artifact cancellation in NIR spectroscopy using wiener filtering</article-title><source>IEEE Trans Biomed Eng</source><year>2005</year><volume>52</volume><fpage>934</fpage><lpage>938</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15887543</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1109/TBME.2005.845243</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wilson</surname><given-names>GF</given-names></name><name><surname>Fisher</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The use of cardiac and eye blink measures to determine flight segment in F4 crews</article-title><source>Aviat Space Environ Med</source><year>1991</year><volume>62</volume><fpage>959</fpage><lpage>962</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1764007</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Izzetoglu</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Izzetoglu</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Bunce</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Ayaz</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Devaraj</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Onaral</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Pourrezaei</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Functional near-infrared neuroimaging</article-title><source>IEEE Transactions on Neural Systems and Rehabilitation Engineering</source><year>2005</year><volume>13</volume><fpage>153</fpage><lpage>159</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16003893</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1109/TNSRE.2005.847377</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>J&#x000f6;bsis</surna